  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="56eb-3301-4cff-63cd" name="Al-Andalus and Granada (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #66 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). Al-Andalus, “the Land of the Vandals”, was conquered by the Arabs from the Visigoths in the early 8th century, leaving only small parts of the North of Spain in Christian hands. It grew to become one of the richest and most cultured parts of Europe and spent the next seven centuries in conflict with the Christian North, gradually losing ground until finally defeated in 1492. The list can be used to create armies from three periods; Early, when the region was mostly united under the Caliphate of Cordoba; Middle, when split into competing petty kingdoms; and late, when only the state of Granada continued to resist. Allies: Al Andalus and Taifa Kingdoms armies may take allies from the North African Berber or Christian Spanish lists. Allies: Nasrid Kingdom armies may take allies from the Medieval Spain army list.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Al-Andalus and Granada - Al Andalus (755 AD-1008 AD)]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: Up to 25%. Cannot take a Christian captain as Army General. Cavalry: Up to 50%. May not take lancers or crossbowmen. At least half the cavalry must be Jinetes. Infantry: Up to 50%. May not take crossbowmen. Allies: Up to 33%. From either Berber or Christian Spanish lists, but not both.
[Al-Andalus and Granada - The Nasrid Kingdom of Granada (1110 AD-1492 AD)]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: Up to 25%. May have warhorse (+16), heavy armour (+1) and lance (+6). Cavalry: Up to 50%. Jinetes may have light armour (+2). May not take Nobles. Infantry: Up to 50% Allies: Up to 50%
[Al-Andalus and Granada - The Taifa Kingdoms (1009-1110 AD)]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: Up to 25%. May have warhorse (+16). Cavalry: Up to 50%. May not take lancers or crossbowmen. At least half the cavalry must be Jinetes. Infantry: Up to 50%. May take only one unit of crossbowmen. Allies: Up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
